<p>Two rules from the book that the slide leaves out: the integrated diagram must include the messages of the <strong>alternative sequences</strong>, not only the main sequence (it is meant to be a <em>complete</em> description of all messages); and it is a <strong>generic</strong> diagram — no sequence numbers, object names not underlined, messages still "simple" (the synchronous/asynchronous decision comes later, slide 31).</p>
